        "Haviland made in America. From 1936 to about 1957 Shenango China of New Castle, Pennsylvania, made dinnerware for Theodore Haviland, marked Theodore Haviland New York and Made in America {src:lehner,travis,lchs}; the trademark office records the mark as registered in 1951, claiming use from 1938 {src:uspto}. That ware is American, not from Limoges.",
        "Limoges made in Ohio. The Limoges China Company of Sebring, Ohio, put Limoges in its marks; threatened with a lawsuit from France, it changed to American Limoges, a mark it filed in 1941 {src:lehner,sebring}.",
